1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,330
This video goes deeper into the CrestApps Wizard:

2
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:09,174
every setting of the Wizard part, how visitors resume where they left off,

3
00:00:09,174 --> 00:00:14,200
who may start and continue a wizard, and the workflow events a wizard raises.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,066
A long form puts visitors off.

5
00:00:21,066 --> 00:00:25,095
A wizard asks for one step at a time, with a progress bar,

6
00:00:25,095 --> 00:00:28,180
and creates content items from the answers.

7
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:33,456
Each step is an ordinary content type, so it has its own fields.

8
00:00:33,456 --> 00:00:36,560
The wizard type holds the steps, in order.

9
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:41,865
A visitor who leaves can come back and continue, and you decide who

10
00:00:41,865 --> 00:00:45,110
may start one and what happens to the answers.

11
00:00:49,311 --> 00:00:54,932
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, edit the type that will host the

12
00:00:54,932 --> 00:00:57,154
wizard, and click Add Parts.

13
00:00:57,154 --> 00:01:00,161
Next to Wizard, click Add and Configure.

14
00:01:00,612 --> 00:01:05,018
Contained content types are the kinds of step this wizard can have.

15
00:01:05,018 --> 00:01:10,148
Choose Content types and tick them, or choose Stereotype to allow every content

16
00:01:10,148 --> 00:01:12,682
type that has a stereotype you type.

17
00:01:13,134 --> 00:01:18,417
Display type is how the steps are shown when the wizard item itself is displayed.

18
00:01:18,417 --> 00:01:22,971
Collapse contained steps shows them collapsed when you edit a wizard.

19
00:01:22,971 --> 00:01:26,978
Requires an authenticated user makes visitors sign in first.

20
00:01:26,978 --> 00:01:32,139
Completion policy decides what happens to the answers when the wizard finishes:

21
00:01:32,139 --> 00:01:37,422
create and publish the content items, create them as drafts, or do not keep them.

22
00:01:37,422 --> 00:01:38,454
Click Save.

23
00:01:42,659 --> 00:01:46,924
Create a content item of the wizard type, give it a title, and

24
00:01:46,924 --> 00:01:49,307
click Add step to add each step.

25
00:01:49,307 --> 00:01:54,199
Each step card has its own fields, which can start with a default value.

26
00:01:54,922 --> 00:01:58,241
The order of the cards is the order of the steps, and you

27
00:01:58,241 --> 00:02:00,085
can drag a card to change it.

28
00:02:00,085 --> 00:02:01,402
Publish the wizard.

29
00:02:05,608 --> 00:02:09,685
A visitor opens the wizard, with a progress bar at the top, fills

30
00:02:09,685 --> 00:02:12,038
in the first step, and clicks Next.

31
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:18,230
Now they are on the second step, and they leave, for example to read something else.

32
00:02:18,894 --> 00:02:23,299
When they open the wizard again, it resumes on the second step, and

33
00:02:23,299 --> 00:02:26,256
Previous still shows their earlier answers.

34
00:02:26,256 --> 00:02:31,324
The wizard remembers the session in the visitor's browser, so nothing is lost.

35
00:02:35,519 --> 00:02:38,459
Two permissions control who can take part:

36
00:02:38,459 --> 00:02:41,093
Start a wizard and Continue a wizard.

37
00:02:41,093 --> 00:02:46,116
Open a role, search for wizard, and you find them under the Wizard category.

38
00:02:46,116 --> 00:02:51,261
The Anonymous role has both by default, so a public wizard works for visitors.

39
00:02:51,261 --> 00:02:56,223
Remove them to restrict a wizard, or tick Requires an authenticated user on

40
00:02:56,223 --> 00:02:59,469
the wizard type to make visitors sign in first.

41
00:03:03,269 --> 00:03:06,793
With Workflows on, a wizard raises four events:

42
00:03:06,793 --> 00:03:13,109
Wizard Started when a new session begins, and Wizard Step Displayed when a step is shown.

43
00:03:13,859 --> 00:03:19,553
Wizard Completed is raised when a session finishes, and Wizard Failed when it fails.

44
00:03:19,553 --> 00:03:22,399
Each can be limited to one wizard type.

45
00:03:23,149 --> 00:03:28,096
Every event carries the session, the wizard type, the current step and the

46
00:03:28,096 --> 00:03:32,609
status, so a workflow can send a welcome email or notify your team.

47
00:03:36,809 --> 00:03:39,689
Event and workshop registrations.

48
00:03:40,439 --> 00:03:42,189
Customer onboarding.

49
00:03:42,939 --> 00:03:45,889
Surveys that are too long for one page.

50
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:49,949
Intake forms that visitors may finish later.

51
00:03:51,949 --> 00:03:57,181
Choose the steps, decide who may take part, and let visitors resume where they stopped.

52
00:03:57,181 --> 00:04:01,457
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

53
00:04:01,457 --> 00:04:02,919
Thanks for watching.

